From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:17:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScript: DOM fixes found by YouTube's Polymer app

- innerHTML of markup starting with a comment gave no nodes at all
  (the fragment parser puts leading comments before the html element,
  and only the first child was looked at): every Polymer template of
  YouTube came out empty.
- Attr is a Node with name, value, localName, namespaceURI, prefix,
  ownerElement (Attr.bnd; attribute nodes had Node's prototype only).
- textContent of an element without text is "" (it was undefined),
  null for the document and doctype.
- List and NamedNodeMap proxies index with the list's own item(): a
  script replacing list.item with i => list[i] (ShadyDOM) looped.
- DOMContentLoaded is fired once (html_begin_conversion runs again
  whenever a script or style sheet added later has loaded); events at
  the Window have an eventPhase; an on<event> handler that is not
  callable is ignored (duk_is_callable).
- Scripts may use the process's stack less a margin (at most 8 MB)
  instead of QuickJS's 1 MB: Polymer elements nest deeper.
